Apple's expected switch to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a> will help accelerate a sharp decline in mini-LED laptop displays, with annual panel shipments forecast to fall roughly 75% between 2025 and 2027, according to <a href="https://counterpointresearch.com/en/insights/oled-gains-momentum-as-notebook-display-market-shifts-toward-premium">Counterpoint Research</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/04/Oled-MackBook-Pros-23.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-891130" /><br/>
Apple's &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models have used mini-LED displays since 2021, but Counterpoint expects notebook panel shipments using the technology to drop 38% in 2026 and another 60% in 2027. Those consecutive declines would leave shipments at approximately a quarter of their 2025 level.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;OLED&zwnj; is heading in the opposite direction. Notebook &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; panel shipments are projected to grow 50% this year and 24% next year, amounting to an 86% increase over 2025. Counterpoint identifies the anticipated &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; and demand for premium AI PCs as drivers, even as the overall notebook display market is expected to shrink 3% in 2026.<br/>
<br/>
The forecast points to a rapid change in manufacturers' display choices. Counterpoint says &zwnj;OLED&zwnj;'s thinner profile, image quality, and improving cost competitiveness are encouraging adoption, with tandem &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; designs and larger production facilities supporting further growth.<br/>
<br/>
For &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; users, the display transition is also expected to bring touch input to the Mac for the first time. Samsung Display is reportedly the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/28/samsung-name-its-price-macbook-pro-oled/">exclusive supplier</a> of the new 14-inch and 16-inch &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; touch panels, manufactured on its 8.6-generation line in Asan, South Korea, according to <em>The Elec</em>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is expected to unveil the &zwnj;OLED&zwnj; &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj; models on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/25/macbook-pro-with-touchscreen-on-wednesday/">Wednesday, October 28</a> at its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/19/apple-pro-and-tell/">"Pro and tell"</a> media experience in Los Angeles. According to <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a>, the laptops will be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/04/oled-macbook-pro-significantly-lighter-rumor/">significantly lighter</a> and replace the display notch with a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>.<br/>
<br/>
